    "body": "Hey! Thanks for the reply - sever code is below. It's a very simple Flask app in Python that gives results like this:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n\t\"items\": [\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\t\"hello\": \"world\"\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t\t...\r\n\t\t{\r\n\t\t\t\"hello\": \"world\"\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo be clear, it does stop reading when it's reached the 2000th item. But I'm looking for a way to pause and resume it any arbitrary point in the stream.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport json\r\nfrom flask import Flask, Response\r\nfrom flask_cors import CORS\r\n\r\n\r\napp = Flask(__name__)\r\nCORS(app)\r\n\r\n\r\n@app.route('/')\r\ndef home():\r\n\r\n    def my_generator():\r\n        yield '{\"items\": ['\r\n        for count in range(1, 2001):\r\n            my_json_object = json.dumps({\"hello\": \"world\"})\r\n            if count == 2000:\r\n                yield my_json_object\r\n            else:\r\n                yield my_json_object + \", \"\r\n        yield ']}'\r\n    return Response(my_generator(), status=200, content_type='application/json')\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == '__main__':\r\n    app.run(debug=True)\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
